 <longdesc><para unique="1091445">This instruction zeroes the destination tile.</para>
  <para unique="1091446">Any attempt to execute the TILEZERO instruction inside an Intel TSX transaction will result in a transaction abort.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>TILEZERO tdest
nbytes := palette_table[palette_id].bytes_per_row
for i in 0 ... palette_table[palette_id].max_rows-1:
	for j in 0 ... nbytes-1:
		tdest.row[i].byte[j] := 0
zero_tilecfg_start()</programlisting>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>TILEZERO	 void _tile_zero(__tile dst);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1091459">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Exceptions">
  <para unique="1091464" format="xIndent1">AMX-E5; see <link unique="1091462" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#77014: 02_Level: 2.10 Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes" xrefstyle="SectionNum&amp;Title(,)">Section 2.10, &#8220;Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes,&#8221;</link> for details.</para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
